SUMMARY:Montclair Earth Day Park Clean Ups
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Earth Week in Montclair by joining our community’s Earth Week Park Clean Ups! Our beautiful Montclair town parks need your help to stay vibrant and healthy. Volunteer with neighbors\, friends\, and family to make a real difference in our local green spaces. This is a perfect family-friendly outdoor activity and a fantastic community service opportunity for students looking to give back to the environment. Bring your gloves and rakes to help keep Montclair parks clean\, safe\, and beautiful!\nWhen: Saturday\, April 25th\, 10 am – 12:30 pm\nWhere: Canterbury\, Crane\, Nishuane\, Porter\, Rand Stream (next to High School Annex)\, Tuers\, and Yantacaw Brook Parks. You’re also welcome to assist at other Montclair green spaces!\nProudly Co-sponsored by: Northeast Earth Coalition and Montclair Parks\, Recreation & Cultural Affairs Advisory Committee\nReady to volunteer? Contact CleanMontclairParks@gmail.com to register or for more information about this important Montclair park clean-up event! \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
