SUMMARY:Earth Day  Montclair Park Clean-Ups
DESCRIPTION:Montclair’s town parks are in need of a little TLC. Join neighbors and friends for an Earth Day Town Park Clean-Up Event\, helping to spruce up our local green spaces. This is a fantastic community service opportunity for students and a rewarding way for families to give back to the environment. Grab your gloves and rakes and help keep our parks beautiful\, safe\, and healthy. \nWhen: Saturday\, April 25th\, 10 am – 12:30 pm\nWhere: Canterbury\, Crane\, Nishuane\, Porter\, Rand Stream (next to High School Annex)\, Tuers and Yantacaw Brook Parks. Feel free to help out at other town parks.\nCo-sponsored by Montclair Parks\, Recreation & Cultural Affairs Advisory Committee and Northeast Earth Coalition \nContact: CleanMontclairParks@gmail.com to register or for information \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
